  "description": "AGSC-08-16 (amended 2026-10-02 for 1.0.0): every shape of the minimum set is detected and a bare run of digits is not. Each string is the concatenation of its `parts`, so that no file of the distribution carries a credential- or number-shaped string a secret scanner would flag; it is checked alone, as one in-scope string of an item outside prov and sources[]; `code` is the code reported for it, or null when the string raises nothing. The positives are an e-mail address, two international numbers, the three North-American forms and a tel: URI; the negatives are a version, a port, an ISBN, a bare run of eleven digits, a date and an address spelled out in words. The numbers are of fictional or reserved forms. Derived by hand from the rule text; how many findings one string raises is not asserted.",
